      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A study of 20 anginal patients demonstrated signs of platelet hyperreactivity: increased platelet aggregation, increased mobilization of Ca2+ from platelet membranes, and increased production of malonic dialdehyde. A short-term treatment with isoptin-120 (360 mg daily) produced a considerable drop in those parameters. It is suggested that the drug's basic effect is due to the inhibition of intracellular calcium redistribution in the platelets of coronary patients."},
